      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Encountered this and found a workaround:\n\n1. Create a group only instance.\n\n2. Open a mutual members profile to invite.\n\nThe \"Send Invite\" button is disabled and there is text that displays \"Can't invite to this instance: This user is not a member of the group.\"\n\n3. Click on their groups \"View All\" button.\n\n4. Click the arrow back to their profile.\n\n5. Now \"Send Invite\" button is enabled.\n\nIt seems like the invite button does not check if the group is mutual until you look at the profiles groups yourself.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-01-04T23:53:29.282Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "As it is right now, I'm not able to invite friends to a group instance - even if they're in the group. So if I throw an event, I just have to guide them through their menu rather than just shooting out invites. The option to send an invite is just greyed out. I feel like it should allow me to invite people to the instance if they're part of the group.",
